Spec: vynilconfig

Purpose:
  Serve the diagnostic API's `vynilconfig` item: one point read of the `vynil` @ConfigMap in the
    server's `vynil_namespace`, that object's string `data` map re-serialized to YAML by
    @serde_yaml::to_string, that text masked through @scrub_yaml over the request `namespace`'s
    and the `vynil_namespace`'s Secrets, and the masked-text-plus-@ScrubStats pair handed back to
    /server/src/server.rs for the `application/yaml` body and the `X-Diag-Redactions` header. An
    absent ConfigMap, an unreadable one and one with empty `data` all answer the empty document
    `---` with zero counters — never an error.

Owns:
  ./vynilconfig.rs

References:
  ../dto.sdd — @ScrubStats is this file's second return slot; the `X-Diag-Redactions` grammar and
    its field-name coupling to /server/src/server.rs @add_scrub_header are owned there.
  ../error.sdd — the exit lane is exactly one variant, @DiagError::YamlError; its `DIAG-500`/`500`
    rendering is owned there.
  ../anonymize.sdd — the @scrub_yaml contract relied on verbatim: raw-text value/regex masking, the
    per-call Secret sweep of both namespaces with silently swallowed list failures, and the
    pass-1-only counter semantics returned here untouched.
  ../state.sdd — the client arriving as the @get_vynil_config argument is the @AppState.client
    cloned by /server/src/server.rs, `vynil_namespace` is @AppState.config.vynil_namespace (default
    `vynil-system`), and `namespace` is the URL `{ns}` segment; the server identity whose own RBAC
    decides whether the ConfigMap read succeeds is specified there.
  /common/src/context.sdd — approved calibration reference; the @kube::Config::infer client-build
    and discovery semantics behind that identity are documented there.

Must:
  Cluster access is exactly one point read: @Api::namespaced(client.clone(), `vynil_namespace`)
    then @Api::get of the fixed object-name literal `vynil`, typed as @k8s_openapi
    @api::core::v1::@ConfigMap — no list, no watch, no @ListParams, no selector anywhere, and the
    object name is never derived from configuration; the request `namespace` never scopes a read.
  Only @ConfigMap::data reaches the output: the @Option @std::collections::@BTreeMap of
    @String-@String pairs is taken through @unwrap_or_default, so @ConfigMap::binary_data,
    @metadata (name, namespace, labels, annotations) and every other field of the object never
    surface, and keys serialize in @BTreeMap ascending order with values verbatim.
  The `---` answer has exactly two producers and both bypass @scrub_yaml entirely — and so issue
    zero Secret-list traffic: the ConfigMap @get failing (the catch-all @Err arm) and the
    ConfigMap carrying absent or empty `data` (the @is_empty short-circuit, returning before any
    serialization). The literal is the three bytes `---`, a valid empty YAML document.
  Non-empty `data` runs the fixed assembly @serde_yaml::to_string → @scrub_yaml(text, client,
    `namespace`, `vynil_namespace`); nothing parses YAML here — this file is a YAML producer whose
    output is then masked as opaque text, and whatever bytes @scrub_yaml returns ship unexamined,
    even if masking broke the document's parseability (the text-lane effects are owned by
    ../anonymize.sdd).
  Redaction is wholly delegated: this file holds no key-name rule, no field allowlist and no notion
    of what is a secret — a config value survives verbatim unless it equals a Secret value
    collected from the two namespaces or matches the JWT/Bearer/PEM regexes, and the @ScrubStats
    returned are @scrub_yaml's counters with no local adjustment.
  The server reads with its own identity and rights; `namespace` reaches @scrub_yaml unvalidated
    and unchecked against the caller — /server/src/server.rs has already enforced the DNS-form
    check, the kind/item allowlists and authentication for the request, but the `vynilconfig` item
    is generic tier (@is_instance_scoped_item answers false in ../authz.rs), so no
    @SubjectAccessReview and no instance-existence check gate this payload.
  The file owns no cache, TTL, informer or global state and performs no write: every
    @get_vynil_config call re-reads the ConfigMap and, on the non-empty path, re-collects Secrets
    through @scrub_yaml.

Depends on:
  @kube `3.1.0` (/Cargo.lock) — @kube::Client and @kube::@api::@Api; only the @namespaced
    constructor and @get with default parameters are used, and the client is cloned once per call
    into the @Api.
  @k8s_openapi `0.27.1` (/Cargo.lock) — @api::core::v1::@ConfigMap as the read type; only its
    @data field is ever touched.
  @serde_yaml `0.9` (/server/Cargo.toml) — @serde_yaml::to_string, the serializer rendering the
    `data` map; no YAML deserialization exists here.
  @crate::anonymize::scrub_yaml in ../anonymize.rs — the infallible mask-and-tally pass over the
    serialized text.
  @crate::dto::@ScrubStats in ../dto.rs — the output shape, plus @ScrubStats::default as the seed
    returned by both `---` paths and as the @Ok pair's second slot.
  @crate::error::@DiagError in ../error.rs — the return lane and the @DiagError::YamlError
    constructor built by the @map_err leg.

Exposes:
  @get_vynil_config — the file's only `pub` item and the whole surface, shaped
    pub async fn @get_vynil_config(client: &@kube::@Client, `vynil_namespace`: &@str,
      `namespace`: &@str) -> @Result<(@std::string::@String, @ScrubStats), @DiagError>,
    doc-commented with an `# Errors` section, reachable as
    @crate::collect::vynilconfig::get_vynil_config through `pub mod vynilconfig;` in ./mod.rs and
    `pub mod collect;` in /server/src/lib.rs.
  No typed configuration model — nothing named like a cluster-config DTO is defined or
    reconstructed here; what is exposed is the raw serialized @ConfigMap::data text of the cluster's
    secret material and nothing else, so secret-bearing values are masked only where the
    @scrub_yaml collection fires and leak elsewhere by ../anonymize.sdd's rule set.
  Sole consumer: the `vynilconfig` arm of /server/src/server.rs @instance_handler, which passes
    (@AppState.client, @AppState.config.vynil_namespace, URL `{ns}`), renders the @Ok text through
    @yaml_response as `200` with content type `application/yaml`, and attaches the tally through
    @add_scrub_header; both `---` paths still get the all-zero redaction header.

Accepts:
  @client — a borrowed @kube::Client cloned once into the @Api; the identity's rights on core/v1
    @ConfigMap in `vynil_namespace` decide whether data is ever seen, and every read failure
    degrades silently (Handles).
  `vynil_namespace` — both the read namespace and @scrub_yaml's second Secret-collection
    namespace; the caller passes @AppState.config.vynil_namespace; taken verbatim with no
    validation, so an empty or wrong value simply misses the object.
  `namespace` — the URL `{ns}` segment, DNS-form-validated only upstream; its single use is as
    @scrub_yaml's primary Secret-collection namespace — no read of this namespace is ever issued.
  No shape precondition on the object: absent `data`, empty `data` and arbitrary key/value
    content are ordinary @Ok inputs.

Returns:
  Non-empty `data`: @Ok of (@masked text, @ScrubStats) — the @serde_yaml rendering of the map
    (ascending keys, scalar `key: value` lines) with the @scrub_yaml masking applied and that
    pass-1 tally attached, so pattern-pass redactions report zero counters on masked text
    (../anonymize.sdd).
  Absent or unreadable ConfigMap, absent or empty `data`: @Ok of (`"---"`, @ScrubStats::default())
    — an empty YAML document, `200`/`application/yaml` and the all-zero header at the caller.

Raises:
  @DiagError::YamlError — the only raisable variant, on @serde_yaml::to_string of the `data` map
    via explicit @map_err, rendered `DIAG-500`/`500` (../error.sdd); for a string-keyed,
    string-valued @BTreeMap the arm is practically unreachable on the locked `0.9` build (Tasks
    `[!]`).
  Not raised despite the doc comment's claim: @DiagError::KubeError never leaves — every
    @kube::Error from the @get is consumed by the catch-all arm.
  No panic path: the file contains no @unwrap, @expect or @panic (the @unwrap_or_default leg
    defaults, never aborts).

Handles:
  Every read failure — `404` absent, RBAC `403`, transport, decode — lands at the same
    (`"---"`, zero) answer the in-file "ConfigMap absent → empty document" comment describes, so a
    server missing ConfigMap get rights reads to clients as a configless cluster (Tasks `[?]`).
  Four wire-identical outcomes: object absent, read refused, `data` @None and `data: {}` all
    render as the empty document with the all-zero redaction header.
  Caller-chosen mask scope on a cluster-wide payload: any authenticated caller names an arbitrary
    DNS-valid `namespace` in the URL (generic tier, nothing binds it to the caller), and that
    choice decides which tenant's Secret values may redact this answer.
  Secret material stored in @ConfigMap::binary_data is outside the contract entirely — never read,
    never decoded, never masked, simply absent from the payload.
  Values that merely look secret by key name (`password: hunter2` with `hunter2` collected
    nowhere) pass through verbatim — masking is value-driven upstream, never key-driven here.

Tasks:
  [ ] No `#[cfg(test)]` module exists in this file and the server crate has no integration test
      files; cover all Scenarios below from these blocks once a cluster double exists
      (dev-dependencies are empty, per ../anonymize.sdd).
  [!] The @DiagError::YamlError lane looks dead: @serde_yaml::to_string over a string/`@BTreeMap`
      of plain strings has no failure mode to map, so the function's only `?` leg never fires and
      the @Err result is unreachable today. Decide with Tasks' doc-comment `[?]` whether the
      signature collapses or the defensive arm stays.
  [?] The catch-all @Err(_) swallows RBAC refusals, transport and decode failures as "absent"
      while the in-file comment pins only the absent case — an RBAC-broken server answers `---`
      exactly like a configless cluster. Decide later whether only `404` degrades and other
      failures surface as @DiagError::KubeError.
  [?] The doc comment promises "the @DiagError raised by the `ConfigMap` read or YAML
      serialization", but read errors never propagate — only the near-unreachable serialization
      arm can. Reconcile the wording with the degradation contract (with the `[!]` above if the
      arm collapses).
  [?] Generic-tier exposure of cluster config: no @SubjectAccessReview gates `vynilconfig`
      (../authz.rs) and the caller-named `namespace` picks the Secret-sweep scope of the mask —
      complementing the Secret-probe oracle deferred in ../anonymize.sdd. Decide later whether
      this item gains its own authorization or whether the mask scope moves to the server
      identity.
  [?] @ConfigMap::binary_data is silently ignored — binary-stored values never surface and never
      scrub on this endpoint. Decide later whether they join the payload or stay out of contract
      deliberately.

Done when:
  Every Scenario below maps to a green test in `server`, the `[?]`/`[!]` decisions above are
    recorded, and `cargo test -p server` with `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and
    `cargo +nightly fmt --check` stays green.

Scenario: Present ConfigMap masks, counts travel, reads stay in vynil namespace
  Given a get of `vynil` in `vynil_namespace` succeeding with `data` entries out of alphabetical
    order, one value equal to a collected Secret value
  When @get_vynil_config runs
  Then exactly one @Api::get is issued and only into `vynil_namespace`, the text is the @serde_yaml
    rendering with ascending keys, the Secret-equal value arrives masked, and the returned
    @ScrubStats are @scrub_yaml's tally untouched
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Every read failure answers the empty document
  Given the ConfigMap @get failing with `404`, with RBAC `403`, and with a transport error
  When @get_vynil_config runs in each case
  Then all three @Ok with (`"---"`, @ScrubStats::default()), the caller answering `200`
    `application/yaml` with `X-Diag-Redactions: distinct=0;occurrences=0`, and no Secret list is
    ever issued because @scrub_yaml never runs
  And @DiagError::KubeError raises never despite the doc comment
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Empty data short-circuits before any masking
  Given a ConfigMap found with `data` @None and another with `data: {}`
  When @get_vynil_config runs
  Then both @Ok (`"---"`, @ScrubStats::default()) with no serialization and no Secret traffic,
    indistinguishable on the wire from the absent-object answer
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: URL namespace steers masking only, never a read
  Given URL `{ns}` `tenant-a` while @AppState.config.vynil_namespace is `vynil-system` and a
    Secrets-carrying `tenant-a`
  When @get_vynil_config runs
  Then the @get hits `vynil-system`, and @scrub_yaml receives `tenant-a` plus `vynil-system` —
    `tenant-a`'s Secret values can redact this cluster-wide payload on the generic tier although
    no object in `tenant-a` is ever read
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Value matching decides what vanishes
  Given `data` holds `db_url` whose value equals a collected Secret, `jwt_header` holding an `eyJ…`
    token, and `password: hunter2` with `hunter2` collected nowhere
  When @get_vynil_config runs
  Then `db_url`'s value is masked and counted, `jwt_header`'s token is masked but the counters stay
    zero (pattern pass is invisible, ../anonymize.sdd), and `password: hunter2` ships verbatim —
    key names earn no masking
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  Pre-scrub text for `data` = {`level`: `info`, `sa_token`: `eyJAAA.BBB.CCC`}: `level: info` then
    the `sa_token` line — ascending keys; after @scrub_yaml the token line reads the marker
    `<anonymized>` while /server/src/server.rs still answers a
    `X-Diag-Redactions: distinct=0;occurrences=0` header because no collected Secret matched
  Empty answer on the wire: body `---`, content type `application/yaml`, header
    `X-Diag-Redactions: distinct=0;occurrences=0`
